& [BoundaryFormation] separates three layers
  + [pure_form] validates supplied machine records without observation
  + [physical_preflight] later opens one root and performs bounded Win32 queries
  + [topology_scanner] later traverses a root and issues a receipt
  + [authority] this explosion reaches only pure_form

& [AtomicRequirementSet] is complete
  + [M2B-PF-001] preserves selected source, official research, completed-work review, and SJS lineage
  + [M2B-PF-002] fixes profile 0.1 and initial target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
  + [M2B-PF-003] validates canonical extended-DOS drive input roots
  + [M2B-PF-004] models exactly open_fault, query_fault, and complete outcomes
  + [M2B-PF-005] reuses strong root identity and canonical volume-GUID final-path semantics
  + [M2B-PF-006] validates complete bounded volume information
  + [M2B-PF-007] validates bounded remote-protocol header information
  + [M2B-PF-008] enforces exact complete-outcome disposition relations
  + [M2B-PF-009] enforces nonzero faults, closed query stages, and no admitted partial evidence
  + [M2B-PF-010] rejects unknown JSON, unknown variants, NUL, blank required text, and resource excess
  + [M2B-PF-011] proves zero Win32, unsafe, filesystem, process, environment, clock, random, network, persistence, fixture, candidate, scanner, and receipt effects
  + [M2B-PF-012] closes focused, global, lint, release, docs, audit, evidence, rollback, registry, and support review

& [ProfileAtom] is exact
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-platform-preflight/0.1
  + [target] is x86_64-pc-windows-msvc
  + [other_target] rejects

& [InputPathAtom] is lexical
  + [prefix] is exactly extended DOS drive syntax
  + [drive] is uppercase A through Z followed by colon and backslash
  + [components] are nonempty and backslash separated
  + [forbidden] is relative, drive-relative, ordinary DOS, UNC, volume GUID, device, NT, forward slash, NUL, dot, dot-dot, repeated separator, and trailing separator
  + [maximum_UTF8_bytes] is 32768
  + [existence] is not checked

& [OutcomeAtom] is closed
  + [open_fault] contains profile, target, input root, and nonzero Win32 error
  + [query_fault] contains profile, target, input root, one query stage, and nonzero Win32 error
  + [complete] contains profile, target, input root, root identity, final volume-GUID path, volume, remote protocol, and disposition
  + [partial_evidence] is absent from both fault shapes

& [QueryStageAtom] is closed
  + [file_id_info] is selected
  + [final_volume_guid_path] is selected
  + [volume_information] is selected
  + [remote_protocol_information] is selected

& [VolumeAtom] is complete
  + [volume_name] may be empty but not contain NUL and is at most 1024 UTF-8 bytes
  + [volume_serial_number] is u32 without permanence claim
  + [maximum_component_length] is 1 through 32767
  + [file_system_flags] is u32 raw evidence
  + [file_system_name] is nonblank, NUL-free, ASCII, and at most 64 bytes

& [RemoteProtocolAtom] is bounded
  + [structure_version] is 1 or 2
  + [structure_size] is 116
  + [protocol] is u32
  + [protocol_major_version] is u16
  + [protocol_minor_version] is u16
  + [protocol_revision] is u16
  + [flags] is u32
  + [reserved_fields] are not admitted

& [DispositionAtom] is relational
  + [eligible_local_ntfs] requires filesystem name exactly NTFS and protocol zero
  + [reject_remote_protocol] requires protocol nonzero regardless of filesystem name
  + [reject_unsupported_file_system] requires protocol zero and filesystem name other than NTFS
  + [query_fault] is indeterminate and has no disposition
  + [open_fault] is indeterminate and has no disposition

& [IdentityAtom] is reused
  + [root_identity] is StrongFileIdentity with 64-bit volume serial and 32-character lowercase file ID hex
  + [final_path] uses the TopologyReceipt 0.2 volume-GUID grammar
  + [identity_lifetime] is scan-local and not permanent
  + [cross_serial_equivalence] between u64 FileIdInfo serial and u32 volume-information serial is not asserted

& [DataDesignModel] is typed evidence
  + [sum_type] ensures a fault cannot carry a complete observation
  + [complete_product] ensures an accepted observation cannot omit a required query value
  + [closed_enums] constrain outcome, query stage, and disposition
  + [shared_identity] prevents semantic drift from TopologyReceipt
  + [shared_final_path_grammar] prevents duplicate path meaning
  + [strict_decoder] combines serde unknown-field rejection and semantic validation

& [ConstraintLedger] is fail closed
  + [C-01] one new safe-Rust module and one lib export are the only production code changes
  + [C-02] no Cargo or lock change
  + [C-03] no windows-sys reference in the new production module
  + [C-04] no unsafe token in the new production module
  + [C-05] no filesystem or OS observation type or function
  + [C-06] no complete record with inconsistent disposition
  + [C-07] no fault record with error zero
  + [C-08] no query fault outside the four closed stages
  + [C-09] no partial query values in fault records
  + [C-10] no unbounded or NUL-bearing text
  + [C-11] no physical, runtime, local-NTFS, or remote-classification claim
  + [C-12] every affected manifest is regenerated after narrative closure

& [FailureModeSet] is explicit
  + [F-01] unsupported profile or target admits
  + [F-02] unsafe lexical input root admits
  + [F-03] malformed strong identity or volume-GUID final path admits
  + [F-04] incomplete volume or remote record admits
  + [F-05] remote protocol is labeled eligible
  + [F-06] non-NTFS local protocol is labeled eligible
  + [F-07] NTFS local protocol is labeled unsupported
  + [F-08] zero error or unknown stage admits
  + [F-09] JSON smuggles unknown fields or variants
  + [F-10] forms are misreported as physical evidence

& [VerificationProgram] is ordered
  + [V-01] prove exact profile and target
  + [V-02] test accepted and rejected extended-DOS root forms
  + [V-03] test open and query faults with strict no-partial shapes
  + [V-04] test exact eligible local NTFS complete record
  + [V-05] test remote and unsupported-filesystem rejections
  + [V-06] test every cross-field disposition contradiction
  + [V-07] test identity, final path, scalar, text, NUL, and JSON boundaries
  + [V-08] statically prove forbidden effect surface absent
  + [V-09] run global debug, overflow-checked release, lint, build, docs, and audit
  + [V-10] regenerate evidence and close solution, proof, review, narrative, and reentry

& [SemanticRefinementTrace] is exact
  + [preflight_form] is supplied evidence validation, not observation
  + [open_fault] means no valid root handle exists for later queries
  + [query_fault] means a handle may have opened but complete evidence was not admitted
  + [complete] means all specified values were supplied and coherent, not that Cantor observed them
  + [eligible] is a pure relation over supplied values, not runtime authorization
  + [protocol_zero] is a declared policy inference with an explicit invalidation condition

& [ConstraintCheckTrace] is grounded
  + [completed_probe] proves declarations only and motivates the next boundary
  + [Microsoft_volume_docs] define complete volume outputs and SMB non-support
  + [Microsoft_final_path_docs] define volume-GUID shape and network-share failure
  + [Microsoft_file_info_docs] bind FileRemoteProtocolInfo and FileIdInfo structures
  + [existing_forms] supply proven strong identity and final-path grammar

& [PruningTrace] removes overreach
  + [pruned] Windows function calls
  + [pruned] handle ownership
  + [pruned] pointer and buffer mechanics
  + [pruned] partial evidence
  + [pruned] broad target support
  + [pruned] recursive topology data
  + [pruned] physical fixture and scanner claims

& [FoldTrace] is seven-fold
  + [fold_1_intent] freeze preflight meaning before observation
  + [fold_2_terms] form, observation, eligibility, runtime authority, and scanner authority are distinct
  + [fold_3_relations] outcome sum type and disposition relations preserve completeness
  + [fold_4_constraints] paths, text, scalars, variants, and effects are bounded
  + [fold_5_failures] ten invalidation paths are explicit
  + [fold_6_verification] ten ordered proof gates are explicit
  + [fold_7_nonclaims] no path, handle, call, local-NTFS fact, scanner, or receipt exists

